/**
 * Seed catalogue generator -> data/cities/mumbai/experiences.jsonl
 *
 * WHY A GENERATOR, NOT A HAND-WRITTEN FILE: reproducible, diffable, and it lets
 * provenance be applied systematically rather than per-record by hand.
 *
 * PROVENANCE HONESTY — READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING A NUMBER.
 *
 * `name`, `category`, `neighbourhood` and `location` are real, verifiable Mumbai
 * places. Coordinates are approximate seeds (~100 m) intended to be snapped to
 * OSM by `scripts/harvest-osm.ts`; the neighbourhood is what the engine actually
 * uses, and it is correct.
 *
 * `durationMin`, `pricePerPerson`, `capacity`, `accessibility` and `kidFriendly`
 * are NOT local knowledge. They are order-of-magnitude ESTIMATES and are marked
 * `inferred` with low confidence, which is what makes the UI show an
 * "AI-inferred" badge on them. This is deliberate: we measured that OSM has
 * opening hours on 16% of Mumbai POIs, wheelchair access on 1% and price on
 * none, and we would rather show a labelled estimate than launder a guess into a
 * fact.
 *
 * BEFORE THE DEMO: Abhijit or Vishwesh must replace the `inferred` fields with
 * real local knowledge and flip them to `curated`. See DATA_SPEC.md §4.
 * The engine deliberately prefers a `curated` fact over an `inferred` one, and
 * `scoring.ts` penalises inferred fields, so leaving these as estimates makes
 * the product look worse rather than better — which is the correct incentive.
 *
 * Run: npx tsx scripts/gen-seed.ts
 */
